Deterministic processing should agree between live consumption and catch-up. Event ordering and late-arrival rules belong to the domain.

> The overarching goal of deterministic processing is that a microservice should produce the same output whether it is processing in real time or catching up to the present time.

Source: [Q11](/lore/durability-bibliography#q11); [B5](/lore/durability-bibliography#b5-building-event-driven-microservices).

## Failure it prevents

Reprocessing the same history changes decisions because time, ordering, or an external answer changed.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Activity` can record an [effect](/lore/effect-basics) result under an engine. `Stream` does not choose event-time ordering, lateness policy, or protect a rebuild from live writes.

Source: `packages/effect/src/workflow/Activity.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Stream.ts`.

## How to check

Replay captured input into a clean target with controlled decisions. Compare output and apply the declared late-event policy. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Old events must still decode](/lore/old-events-must-still-decode), [Pure cores reduce timeline coupling](/lore/pure-cores-reduce-timelines).

